# Host tests — no pack-name contracts

Index: [external plugins vs host](./forja-external-plugins-host.mdc)

## Plugins are external

JavaScript packs under `plugins/**` are **developed and shipped outside the Flutter host**.
Users may install different hubs, rename tabs, omit packs, or fork providers.
The host must **not** behave as if `anime`, `kisskh`, `anilist`, `hianime`, or any other
**shipped** id/slot/type is guaranteed to exist.

Pack knowledge lives in packs. Host code and **host tests** prove generic contracts only.

---

## Forbidden in `apps/forja/test/**`

| Do not | Why |
|--------|-----|
| Assert a **shipped plugin id** exists in manifest (`kisskh`, `videasy`, `hianime`, …) | Pack inventory, not host behavior |
| Assert **hub slot / tab ids** as behavioral contracts (`anime`, `asian_drama`, `arabic`) | User may ship `my_hub` instead |
| Use `loadAllForjaHqPlugins()` / repo `plugins/**` manifest as **oracle** for categories, registry, or panel logic | Couples host CI to one pack tree |
| Hardcode pack **type tokens** in host expectations (`expect(types, ['anime'])` from real manifest) | Types come from manifest; host reads them generically |
| Test “does our anime hub work” inside the Flutter test suite | Belongs in pack tests or manual QA |

**Wrong:** `expect(byId('kisskh').types, ['drama'])` after loading providers manifest.

**Wrong:** `expect(PluginRegistry.officialPackIds, contains('forjahq-anime'))` as proof host routing works.

**Right:** `EnginePlugin.fromJson({'id': 'test-provider-a', 'types': ['foo']})` → `panelCategoryFromPlayingPlugin` → `'foo'`.

---

## Allowed in host tests

- **Synthetic fixtures** — arbitrary plugin ids (`test-provider-a`, `hub-plugin-x`), arbitrary type tokens (`foo`, `bar`, `movie`, `tv`), fake manifest JSON inline.
- **Generic mechanics** — `forjaHqSlot('…/hubs/any_slot/manifest.json')` returns `'any_slot'`; envelope parse from **checked-in JSON fixtures** where ids are **test data**, not “the app ships this hub”.
- **Structural constants only** when testing the constant itself (e.g. `EngineCategories.movie` for TMDB defaults) — not tied to a pack name.
- **Opaque passthrough** — `panelCategoryFor(panelCategory: 'anything')` returns `'anything'`; no claim that `'anything'` is a real hub.

---

## Where pack contract tests go

| Layer | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Provider JS behavior, upstream URLs, manifest inventory | `plugins/**` tests, pack CI, or env-gated integration (explicitly labeled **pack**, not host) |
| Host generic contracts | `apps/forja/test/**` with synthetic fixtures only |

When adding host tests after engine/catalog changes: **grep the test for shipped plugin ids and hub slot names**. If the assertion would break when a user removes or renames a pack, it does not belong in the host suite.

